course: dictionary
lesson: 4717
title: Hooray for feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are shouted, not written in a sentence. «Supper's here at last, hooray!» Hooray is an interjection: a word that shows a feeling, often with an exclamation mark, and it can stand on its own.
explain: Look at what happens before the word to find the feeling. Toad was sobbing about his hardships, then he heard the chink of dishes. The word hooray shows that he has suddenly become very happy, so it must be a word of joy.
explain: Hooray can also be spelled hurray or hurrah, and all three mean the same. You can also use it to cheer for someone, as in «hooray for Sam!».
fact: Hooray is an interjection, a word that shows a strong feeling.
fact: «Hooray» means a shout of joy, excitement, or cheering for someone.
fact: Hooray can also be spelled hurray or hurrah.
fact: «Hip hip hooray!» is a group cheer, often shouted at parties and sports matches.
fact: In UK informal speech, a «Hooray Henry» is a loud, rich young man who shows off, and the phrase is said in a mocking way.
exercise: «Supper's here at last, hooray!» What feeling does hooray show? | Anger at being kept waiting | Cold and wet | Sleepy and bored | *Joy and excitement
exercise: Toad sobbed about his hardships, then cried «hooray». What changed? | He fell asleep | Fear of the dark | He was given a hard job | *He heard that supper was ready, so he became happy
exercise: Mo calls his cousin a «Hooray Henry». What does he mean? | A kind teacher | A brave hero who saves the day | *A loud, rich young man who shows off | A small bird
test: The Rat cried «Hooray!» and then «Hooray-oo-ray-oo-ray-oo-ray!» What does the Rat show? | Tiredness | Fear of the dark | Anger | *Great happiness
test: Which word is another spelling of hooray? | Sob | Whisper | Drooped | *Hurrah
exam: The Rat «fell to executing a feeble jig in the snow». What is a jig? | A small bird | A cold, wet winter | A loud shout | *A lively hopping dance
